# Every environment variable the gate battery is allowed to see, one KEY=VALUE
# per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Until 2026-08-17 the local runner inherited the whole
# invoking shell, so the verdict of the `local-gates` status was a function of
# (commit, operator) rather than of the commit alone, and nothing declared or
# recorded the operator half. What a CI container actually gave was not Linux
# and not the cloud: it was an environment built from a reviewed file instead of
# inherited from a person. This file is that reviewed file.
#
# Default deny, declared allow. Anything not named here is stripped before the
# battery runs, and the number stripped is printed and written into the receipt.
#
# THE ATTACK THIS CLOSES, demonstrated on the sibling repository on 2026-08-17
# rather than reasoned about: a file named sitecustomize.py containing
# `os._exit(0)`, placed in any directory on PYTHONPATH, makes every python3
# process exit 0 before it runs a single line of the code under test. Measured:
# the suite produced ZERO bytes of output and returned 0. The tree guard cannot
# see it, because the guard reads `git status --untracked-files=no` and the
# poison file is untracked, or outside the repository altogether. A battery of
# 52 commands, 34 of which begin with python3, turns green in one step.
#
# THE INHERITED MINIMUM is not listed here because it is not repository policy:
# PATH, HOME, TMPDIR and the locale identify the machine. The runner passes them
# through and records them in the receipt. Everything else starts empty.
#
# TO ADD A VARIABLE: name it here with the value the battery should see, and say
# in a comment why the battery needs it. A variable that changes what a check
# MEASURES belongs in this file or nowhere. Setting it in a shell profile puts
# the verdict back under the operator's feet, which is the defect this closes.

# The session cap otherwise refuses the battery's own subprocesses. Carried here
# because scripts/local-gates.sh used to set it inline on the command, which is
# the same undeclared-environment problem in a smaller box.
BROTHERMODE_SESSION_CAP=99

# Byte-compilation off. A stale .pyc has already served deleted code to this
# project once: a same-length edit reverted inside one second is invisible to
# the (mtime, size) check the interpreter uses, so it kept running the code that
# was no longer on disk. A verification run must read the tree, not a cache of
# an earlier one.
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1

# DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and each absence is the point rather than an omission:
#
#   PYTHONPATH            the sitecustomize.py attack above. An inherited
#                         PYTHONPATH can also shadow a module under test with
#                         one from another checkout, which makes a green battery
#                         a statement about the wrong code.
#
#   BROTHERMODE_VAULT     seven read sites. Points the tooling at an external
#                         Obsidian vault, whose contents are facts about the
#                         operator's week rather than about this commit.
#
#   BROTHERMODE_ROOT      five read sites. Re-points the tool at another tree,
#                         so the battery would score a different checkout and
#                         report the verdict against this one.
#
#   BROTHERMODE_REGISTRIES, BM_FENCE_SESSION_ID, BM_FENCE_STRICT
#                         fence behaviour belongs to the session that set it,
#                         not to the commit under test.
#
#   BROTHERMODE_TEST_TIMEOUT, BROTHERMODE_TEST_LOCK_TIMEOUT
#                         a timeout raised from outside can turn a hang into a
#                         pass, or lowered can turn a slow machine into a red
#                         battery. Either way the verdict stops being about the
#                         code.
#
#   BM_WRITE_L04_EVIDENCE, BM_WRITE_E4_EVIDENCE, BM_APPROVAL_RECEIPT
#                         these make suites WRITE into the checkout. The runner
#                         refuses to report when the run modified tracked files,
#                         so an inherited one turns a green battery into a
#                         refusal, at best.
